BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
CATEGORIES:Parsha
SUMMARY:Parshas Nitzavim-Vayeilech / פָּרָשַׁת נִצָּבִים
 ־וַיֵּלֶךְ
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260906
UID:hebcal-20260905-b7fe4e02
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:In Nitzavim (“Standing”)\, Moses addresses the Israelites\
 , emphasizing the importance of following God’s covenant and of not wors
 hiping other gods. He describes the process of repentance and returning to
  God\, and stresses that God’s commandments are achievable and “not in
  the heavens.”\n Vayelekh (“He Went”) opens as Moses tells the peopl
 e of Israel that he will not lead them into the land of Israel and that Jo
 shua will take over. He instructs the people to gather and read Torah publ
 icly every seven years. At God’s command\, Moses writes a poem bearing w
 itness to God’s covenant with the people of Israel.\n\nTorah: Deuteronom
 y 29:9-31:30\nHaftarah: Isaiah 61:10-63:9 | Seventh Haftarah of Consolatio
 n\n\nhttps://hebcal.com/s/5786/51d?uc=ical-diaspora-september-2026
END:VEVENT
